# Hardware Store Stock Control

Stock management app for a hardware store (Ferretería Gastón): sales are registered only to decrement stock.
`plan.md` is the source of truth for scope and priorities; check it before adding features.

## Stack

| Layer    | Tech                          | Hosting               |
| -------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------- |
| Frontend | React + Vite + Tailwind CSS   | GitHub Pages (static) |
| Backend  | Node.js + NestJS + TypeScript | Render (free tier)    |
| Database | PostgreSQL                    | Supabase (free tier)  |
| ORM      | Prisma                        | —                     |

## Repository layout

- `frontend/` — React app
- `backend/` — NestJS API, Prisma schema in `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`

## Language

- All code in English: identifiers, DB tables/columns, comments, commit messages, API error messages.
- Only user-facing UI text is in Spanish (Argentina).

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const precioVenta = producto.precio; // precio final
throw new BadRequestException('Stock insuficiente');

// ✅ GOOD
const salePrice = product.salePrice;
throw new BadRequestException('Insufficient stock');
```

## Scope

- Out of scope: payments, invoices/receipts and AFIP/ARCA. Don't add payment methods, invoice models or AFIP dependencies.
- Prices are informative (weekly report totals); many products have price 0 and must still be sellable.
- Prefer free-tier-friendly solutions; no paid services without asking.
